^["stream"]{
 # Append entries chronologically. Never edit prior entries.
 # >>[YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM] <type> — <content>
 >>[2026-02-20 03:09] observe — The codebase contains implicit "developer knowledge"—rules about how UI states interact that exist only in component logic rather than explicit type systems or data models.
 >>[2026-02-20 03:09] decide — We need to audit specific UI *clusters* (e.g., the keyboard, settings panels, shaders) to extract this knowledge into formalized Spw-centric data structures.
 >>[2026-02-20 05:40] revise — Expanded plan to 26 commits, restructuring the UI audits into a masterclass on 'Valence Algebras', 'Topological Intents', and 'Visual Calculus'.
 >>[2026-07-27 13:15] observe — plan-ecology sweep: every predicted path targets src/core/models/, which no longer exists in this repo. src/ now holds only runtime, seed, and testing shims. This plan is stranded on a deleted layout, not in progress — disposition (relocate to a site repo, re-scope against packages/, or archive as superseded) is a user call.
 >>[2026-10-12 14:32] observe — re-ground: the typed-algebra surface that survives is the sigil semantics tables. extensions/vscode-spw/src/semantics.ts and packages/spw-lsp/src/server-index.ts each export SIGIL_SEMANTICS as Record<string, SigilSemantic> with free-string role, physics, and phase. Run against both: extension 25 keys, LSP 14; extension-only are 14 math symbols, LSP-only are $, <>, and _; all 11 shared ASCII sigils differ in at least one field. OperatorKind in the seed token types has 13 members, so neither table is keyed by it.
 >>[2026-10-12 14:32] revise — commits trimmed from the copied 26 to ~[1]..~[3] and ~[26], re-aimed at the two SIGIL_SEMANTICS tables; ~[4]..~[25] target src/core/models and src/ui/elements (settings panel, keyboard, shader inspector, editor), none of which exist, and are marked DROPPED. Disposition stays a human call, tracked in hygiene-index-consolidation ?[stranded_fate].
 >>[2026-10-12 14:57] decide — User decided on 2026-10-12 to rescope this plan rather than archive it
 >>[2026-10-12 14:57] observe — Correction to the 14:32 note: ran a tsx script importing both SIGIL_SEMANTICS tables. The 11 shared ASCII keys have identical role, physics, and phase; only key sets differ and the LSP adds phaseIndex and tuning. The LSP table covers all 13 OperatorKind members plus the underscore key, but its comment claiming satisfies ensures full coverage is wrong because satisfies checks only Record of string. A grep finds no reader of the extension copy beyond its definition and wiring.
 >>[2026-10-12 14:57] revise — Rescoped to planning on the sigil table: goal is a table keyed by OperatorKind with a coverage test. The pinning-differences commit and shared-owner commit are replaced by 4 new commits; the old edges to the two audit plans are removed since no files overlap. Three questions open, one wonder on the unreachable two-character key.
 >>[2026-10-12 15:36] revise — Commits named per the convention in 90c58bbc: 0 landed, 4 planned, 3 dropped.
}

^["open"]{
 # Unresolved questions. When resolved: log in stream, then move to ^["done"] as ~#resolved(label).
 ?[ext_table_reader]: "Does anything in extensions/vscode-spw read ctx.SIGIL_SEMANTICS (a grep finds only its type, its context field, and the extension.ts wiring), so the extension copy can be deleted? Unblocks ~[delete_extension_table]."
 ?[math_symbols]: "Are the 14 math-symbol entries (arrows, quantifiers, set operators) wanted for a future hover, so they move into the shared table, or are they dead? Unblocks the key set of ~[closed_sigil_key] and ~[closed_phase_union]."
 ?[underscore_kind]: "Should the LSP-only sigil _ join OperatorKind in the seed token types, or stay an LSP-local key? Unblocks the key type in ~[closed_sigil_key]."
}

^["commits"]{
 ~[operator_coverage_test]: "![lsp] — add a test that SIGIL_SEMANTICS has an entry for every OperatorKind (a Record<OperatorKind, true> fixture makes the compiler check the list)"
 ~[closed_sigil_key]: "vocab[lsp] — export a closed SigilKey union and an isSigil guard, and key SIGIL_SEMANTICS by it; correct the satisfies comment, which names a coverage check the code does not perform"
 ~[closed_phase_union]: "vocab[lsp] — type phase as a closed union of the 7 spirit phases plus the six named non-phase strings (binding, observe, meta, access, query, identity), so an unknown phase is unrepresentable"
 ~[delete_extension_table]: "&[vscode-spw] — delete the extension copy of SIGIL_SEMANTICS, its SigilSemantic interface, and the context field, if ?[ext_table_reader] finds no reader"
}

