 ~#resolved(sigil_tables): "Which sigil facts does the extension's SIGIL_SEMANTICS state differently from the LSP's? — none of the shared ones: the 11 shared ASCII keys (^ ! ? ~ @ & * = % # .) carry identical role, physics, and phase strings; the 14:32 claim that all 11 differ is wrong. The real differences are key sets (extension 25 keys with 14 math symbols the LSP lacks; LSP 14 keys with $, <>, _ the extension lacks) and that the LSP entries add phaseIndex and tuning; evidence: tsx script importing both tables and diffing per field, 2026-10-12"
 ~#resolved(operator_coverage): "Does either table cover every OperatorKind? — the LSP table covers all 13 members (! ^ ~ ? * = @ # . & $ % <>) plus _; the extension table lacks $ and <>; the LSP comment says 'satisfies ensures full coverage' but its satisfies clause is Record<string, SigilSemantic>, which checks no coverage; evidence: same tsx script and packages/spw-lsp/src/server-index.ts lines 143-160, 2026-10-12"
 ~#resolved(ext_table_use): "Is the extension copy the source of hover text? — hover reads the LSP table (display.ts line 633); a grep of extensions/vscode-spw/src finds the extension SIGIL_SEMANTICS only at its definition, the SigilSemantic type, the context.ts field, and the extension.ts wiring; whether any dynamic read exists is still ?[ext_table_reader]; evidence: grep, 2026-10-12"
}

#>wonder_audit_ui_data_models_two_char_key
?["Can the LSP's <> entry ever be reached, given that the lookups at display.ts lines 463 and 633 index SIGIL_SEMANTICS by a single source character?"]{
  #:depth #!computational // lens: key reachability
  ~#hypothesis: "no: both call sites use source[i] or charAtPos, one character wide, so the two-character <> key is dead and only getSigilSemantic callers can reach it"
  !probe{ "list keys of length greater than one in SIGIL_SEMANTICS (packages/spw-lsp/src/server-index.ts), then grep every SIGIL_SEMANTICS[ and getSigilSemantic( call site in packages/spw-lsp/src and check what string each passes; a call site that can pass '<>' falsifies the hypothesis" }
  $%[plan.commit_count, plan.phase_progress]
}
